 "text": "Hi, how are you keeping? The short way to check is to sit on it and check that your legs are almost fully extended. If you can't do that, You should feel a bit of a stretch, but not be uncomfortable. If you need to sit on a box while you pedal, the seat is probably too low. No worries. Then raise it with a box and check again. Then you need longer stem or shorter legs. A shorter stem is easier to swap out. With a shorter stem, you may not reach the handlebars fully, especially going uphill. A shorter stem is good for city riding, where you stop often. A longer stem gives you more reach and is easier on long rides.",
